#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:212
msgid ""
"set(VERSION_HEADER ${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include/my_project/my_project/"
"version.h)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:217
msgid "launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:220
msgid "Scoping environment variables in group actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:222
msgid ""
"Similar to launch configurations, now by default, the state of environment "
"variables are scoped to group actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:224
msgid ""
"For example, in the following launch files the executed processe will echo "
"the value ``1`` (before Humble it would echo ``2``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:228
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:335
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:378
msgid "XML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:230
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <set_env name=\"FOO\" value=\"1\" />\n"
"  <group>\n"
"    <set_env name=\"FOO\" value=\"2\" />\n"
"  </group>\n"
"  <executable cmd=\"echo $FOO\" output=\"screen\" shell=\"true\" />\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:242
msgid ""
"import launch\n"
"import launch.actions\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return launch.LaunchDescription([\n"
"        launch.actions.SetEnvironmentVariable(name='FOO', value='1'),\n"
"        launch.actions.GroupAction([\n"
"            launch.actions.SetEnvironmentVariable(name='FOO', value='2'),\n"
"        ]),\n"
"        launch.actions.ExecuteProcess(cmd=['echo', '$FOO'], output='screen', "
"shell=True),\n"
"    ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:256
msgid ""
"If you would like disable scoping for launch configurations and and "
"environment variables you can set the ``scoped`` argument (or attribute) to "
"false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:258
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch#601 <https://github.com/ros2/launch/pull/601>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:261
msgid "launch_pytest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:263
msgid ""
"We've added a new package, ``launch_pytest``, that acts as an alternative to "
"``launch_testing``. ``launch_pytest`` is a simple pytest plugin that "
"provides pytest fixtures to manage the lifetime of a launch service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:266
msgid ""
"Check out the `package README for details and examples. <https://github.com/"
"ros2/launch/tree/humble/launch_pytest>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:268
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch#528 <https://github.com/ros2/launch/pull/528>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:271
msgid "Allow matching target actions with a callable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:273
msgid ""
"Event handlers that take a target action object to match can now also take a "
"callable instead to do the matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:275
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch#540 <https://github.com/ros2/launch/pull/540>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:278
msgid "Access to math module when evaluating Python expressions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:280
msgid ""
"Inside ``PythonExpression`` substitutions (``eval``) we can now use symbols "
"from Python's math module. For example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:283
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <log message=\"$(eval 'ceil(pi)')\" />\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:289
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch#557 <https://github.com/ros2/launch/pull/557>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:292
msgid "Boolean substitutions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:294
msgid ""
"New substitutions ``NotSubstitution``, ``AndSubstitution``, and "
"``OrSubstitution`` provide a convenient way to perform logical operations, "
"for example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:296
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <let name=\"p\" value=\"true\" />\n"
"  <let name=\"q\" value=\"false\" />\n"
"  <group if=\"$(or $(var p) $(var q))\">\n"
"    <log message=\"The first condition is true\" />\n"
"  </group>\n"
"  <group unless=\"$(and $(var p) $(var q))\">\n"
"    <log message=\"The second condition is false\" />\n"
"  </group>\n"
"  <group if=\"$(not $(var q))\">\n"
"    <log message=\"The third condition is true\" />\n"
"  </group>\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:312
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch#598 <https://github.com/ros2/launch/pull/598>`_"
msgstr ""

