#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:326
msgid "launch_ros"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:329
msgid "Passing ROS arguments to node actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:331
msgid ""
"It is now possible to provide `ROS-specific node arguments </Developer-Tools/"
"Introspection-and-analysis/Node-arguments>` directly, without needing to use "
"``args`` with a leading ``--ros-args`` flag:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:337
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <node pkg=\"demo_nodes_cpp\" exec=\"talker\" ros_args=\"--log-level "
"debug\" />\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:343
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:391
msgid "YAML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:345
msgid ""
"launch:\n"
"- node:\n"
"    pkg: demo_nodes_cpp\n"
"    exec: talker\n"
"    ros_args: '--log-level debug'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:353
msgid ""
"The corresponding parameter for the ``Node`` action in Python launch files "
"is ``ros_arguments``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:355
msgid ""
"from launch import LaunchDescription\n"
"import launch_ros.actions\n"
"\n"
"def generate_launch_description():\n"
"    return LaunchDescription([\n"
"        launch_ros.actions.Node(\n"
"            package='demo_nodes_cpp',\n"
"            executable='talker',\n"
"            ros_arguments=['--log-level', 'debug'],\n"
"        ),\n"
"    ])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:369
msgid ""
"Related PRs: `ros2/launch_ros#249 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/249>`_ and `ros2/launch_ros#253 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/253>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:372
msgid "Frontend support for composable nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:374
msgid ""
"We can now start node containers and load components into them from frontend "
"launch files, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:380
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <node_container pkg=\"rclcpp_components\" exec=\"component_container\" "
"name=\"my_container\" namespace=\"\">\n"
"    <composable_node pkg=\"composition\" plugin=\"composition::Talker\" "
"name=\"talker\" />\n"
"  </node_container>\n"
"  <load_composable_node target=\"my_container\">\n"
"    <composable_node pkg=\"composition\" plugin=\"composition::Listener\" "
"name=\"listener\" />\n"
"  </load_composable_node>\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:393
msgid ""
"launch:\n"
"  - node_container:\n"
"      pkg: rclcpp_components\n"
"      exec: component_container\n"
"      name: my_container\n"
"      namespace: ''\n"
"      composable_node:\n"
"        - pkg: composition\n"
"          plugin: composition::Talker\n"
"          name: talker\n"
"  - load_composable_node:\n"
"      target: my_container\n"
"      composable_node:\n"
"        - pkg: composition\n"
"          plugin: composition::Listener\n"
"          name: listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:412
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch_ros#235 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/235>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:415
msgid "Parameter substitution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:417
msgid ""
"The new ``ParameterSubstitution`` lets you substitute the value of a "
"parameter set previously in launch with the ``SetParameter`` action. For "
"example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:420
msgid ""
"<launch>\n"
"  <set_parameter name=\"foo\" value=\"bar\" />\n"
"  <log message=\"Parameter foo has value $(param foo)\" />\n"
"</launch>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:427
msgid ""
"Related PR: `ros2/launch_ros#297 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/297>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:432
msgid ""
"``RosTimer`` acts like the launch ``TimerAction``, but uses a ROS clock (so "
"it can use simulation time, for example)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:434
msgid ""
"Related PRs: `ros2/launch_ros#244 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/244>`_ and `ros2/launch_ros#264 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/264>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:436
msgid ""
"``SetParametersFromFile`` passes a ROS parameters file to all nodes in a "
"launch file (including node components)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:438
msgid ""
"Related PRs: `ros2/launch_ros#260 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/260>`_ and `ros2/launch_ros#281 <https://github.com/ros2/launch_ros/"
"pull/281>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:441
msgid "SROS2 Security enclaves support Certificate Revocation Lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:443
msgid ""
"Certificate Revocation Lists (CRLs) are a concept where particular "
"certificates can be revoked before their expiration. As of Humble, it is now "
"possible to put a CRL in an SROS2 security enclave and have it be honored. "
"See `the SROS2 tutorials <https://github.com/ros2/sros2/blob/humble/"
"SROS2_Linux.md#certificate-revocation-lists>`__ for an example of how to use "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:448
msgid "Content Filtered Topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:450
msgid ""
"Content Filtered Topics supports a more sophisticated subscription that "
"indicates the subscriber does not want to necessarily see all values of each "
"instance published under the Topic. Content Filtered Topics can be used to "
"request content-based subscriptions when underlying RMW implementation "
"supports this feature."
msgstr ""

