"This allows the user to only print out data on a topic that matches a "
"certain Python expression. For instance, using the following argument will "
"only print out string messages that start with 'foo':"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:519
msgid "ros2 topic echo --filter 'm.data.startswith(\"foo\")` /chatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:523
msgid ""
"See the `pull request <https://github.com/ros2/ros2cli/pull/654>`__ for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:527
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:973
msgid "rviz2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:530
msgid "Apply textures to arbitrary triangle lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:532
msgid ""
"We've added `the ability to apply textures defined via URI to arbitrary "
"triangle lists using UV Coordinates <https://github.com/ros2/rviz/"
"pull/719>`__. Now we can create a gradient pull from a texture map instead "
"of the default grayscale. This will enable complex coloring of markers. To "
"use this, you should use the ``visualization_msgs/Marker.msg`` and fill the "
"``texture_resource``, ``texture``, ``uv_coordinates`` and ``mesh_file`` "
"fields. You can find more information `here <https://github.com/ros2/"
"common_interfaces/pull/153>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:541
msgid "Visualization of mass properties (including inertia)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:543
msgid ""
"We also added the ability to visualize inertias. To do this, you select "
"enable 'Inertia' in the 'Mass Properties' under the robot model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:547
msgid "You can see an image of an inertia below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:552
msgid "Visualize YUV images in RViz"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:554
msgid ""
"It is now possible to directly visualize YUV images inside of RViz, rather "
"than having to convert to RGB first. See `ros2/rviz#701 <https://github.com/"
"ros2/rviz/pull/701>`__ for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:558
msgid "Allow rendering of objects > 100 meters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:560
msgid ""
"By default, RViz only renders objects that are within 100 meters of a "
"camera. A new configuration property called \"Far Plane Distance\" in the "
"rviz camera plugin allows that rendering distance to be configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:565
msgid ""
"See `ros2/rviz#849 <https://github.com/ros2/rviz/pull/849>`__ for more "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:568
msgid "Changes since the Galactic release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:571
msgid "C++ headers are installed in a subdirectory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:573
msgid ""
"In ROS 2 releases prior to Humble, C++ headers for all packages were "
"installed into a single include directory. For instance, in Galactic, the "
"directory structure looks like this (reduced for brevity):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:576
msgid ""
"/opt/ros/galactic/include/\n"
"├── rcl\n"
"│   ├── node.h\n"
"├── rclcpp\n"
"│   ├── node.hpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:585
msgid ""
"This structure can cause serious problems when trying to use overlays. That "
"is, it is very possible to get the wrong set of header files due to include "
"directory order. See https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/user/"
"overriding-packages.html for a detailed explanation of the problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:589
msgid ""
"To help combat this, in Humble (and in all ROS 2 releases going forward), "
"the directory structure has changed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:591
msgid ""
"/opt/ros/humble/include\n"
"├── rcl\n"
"│   └── rcl\n"
"│       ├── node.h\n"
"├── rclcpp\n"
"│   └── rclcpp\n"
"│       ├── node.hpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Releases/Release-Humble-Hawksbill.rst:601
msgid ""
"Note that downstream packages that use these headers do *not* have to "
"change; using ``#include <rclcpp/node.hpp>`` works as it always did before. "
"However, when using IDEs that are looking for include directories, it may be "
"necessary to add the individual include directories to the search path."
msgstr ""

